Both documents described the retired pregnant/SLOT2 architecture as
normative. The implemented item 4 no longer uses a SLOT2 carrier, stock
bootm, an autonomous Linux stage2 or a Vanilla FIP/BL2 replacement.

Add a status banner to the top of each document and a normative section
grounded in the current code:

- MD_VANILLA_HANDOFF.md section 21 — the direct path, the single y/N it
  authorizes, the migration state machine as it exists in cmd/ursusubi.c,
  the identity/bootloader outcome, the revised destructive boundary and
  rollback model, and a per-section map of what no longer applies.
- v5.45_VANILLA_INITRAMFS.md section 19 — the same change as a normative
  amendment, listing which clauses of the redaction are suspended and
  which stay in force.

The pregnant/SLOT2 sections are kept rather than deleted: they remain the
record of the decisions and the hardware facts, and the R&D line still
backs the negative guards in selftest_item4_direct_ubi.py.

No HW PASS is claimed for the STOCK->UBI transaction; the first run is
destructive. docs/HW_TEST_ITEM4_RU.md is flagged as still describing the
old checkpoints.

